# Database And API Standards

Use Supabase/Postgres-compatible schemas unless a repo already has a justified alternative.

Use migrations. Do not hand-edit production schemas.

Prefer tenant-scoped tables and explicit `tenant_id` fields when the product is multi-tenant.

Preserve RLS and audit patterns where already present.

API endpoints should be minimal and explicit — build only the contracts the current work requires.

Required entities, contracts, and schemas are defined by the target product's own specification (PRD, program manual, or ADRs) — do not assume any entity list from another product applies here. If a cross-system contract changes, update the relevant local planning, template, or contract artifacts before implementation proceeds.
